statement:
A trait here is $S=\operatorname{Spec}R$ for a discrete valuation ring: a Noetherian local domain of dimension one whose maximal ideal is principal. A complete strictly henselian trait has $R$ complete for its maximal-ideal topology and henselian with separably closed residue field (henselian means that every simple root over the residue field of a monic polynomial over $R$ lifts to a root over $R$). Mixed characteristic means that $\operatorname{Frac}R$ has characteristic zero and the residue field has positive characteristic.

Let $R$ be a complete strictly henselian Noetherian regular local ring of mixed characteristic $(0,p)$, with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$, residue field $k$, and dimension $d\geq1$ [def-weil-regular-scheme, def-weil-pbc-henselian-terminology, def-weil-pbc-adic-completion, def-weil-residue-field, def-weil-pbc-krull-dimension-ring]. Fix a prime $\ell$ invertible in $R$ and a regular system of parameters $t_1,\ldots,t_d$ (a minimal generating set of $\mathfrak m$, forming a regular sequence [def-weil-pbc-regular-sequence]). There exist a complete strictly henselian mixed-characteristic trait $S=\operatorname{Spec}C$, with residue field $k$ and $\ell$ invertible, a small directed set $I$, and a compatible inverse system of pairs $Z_i\hookrightarrow V_i$ with affine transition maps, such that:
(i) each $V_i$ is integral regular affine, flat and of finite type over $S$ [def-pc-integral-scheme, def-weil-flat-morphism, def-weil-finite-type-morphism];
(ii) each $Z_i$ is a regular affine $\mathbf F_p$-scheme, and $Z_i\hookrightarrow V_i$ is cut out by a compatible regular sequence $t_{i,1},\ldots,t_{i,d}$ of length $d$ [def-weil-closed-immersion];
(iii) the inverse limit of these pairs is $\operatorname{Spec}k\hookrightarrow\operatorname{Spec}R$, with $t_{i,a}$ mapping to $t_a$.
Here affine spectra have the meaning of [def-weil-affine-spectrum]; each affine $V_i$ is quasi-projective over $S$, since its finite algebra generators give a closed immersion into an affine space, which is open in projective space.

